---
description: Controller / service / repository separation and Zod validation for the API layers
globs: apps/api/src/{routes,controllers,services,repositories,models,validators}/**/*.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

# API layers

| Layer | File | Does | Must not |
|---|---|---|---|
| Routes | `*.routes.ts` | Map verb + path (from `API_ROUTES`) to controller | Contain logic |
| Controller | `*.controller.ts` | Parse input with Zod, call one service method, send `ApiSuccess<T>` | Contain business rules, touch models, branch on domain state |
| Service | `*.service.ts` | Business rules, orchestration, throw `ApiError` | Import Express types or Mongoose models |
| Repository | `*.repository.ts` | All DB access via the Mongoose model | Contain business rules or know about HTTP |
| Validator | `*.validator.ts` | Zod schemas for body/params/query | — |

- Services return shared DTOs (from `@umc/shared`), mapping from lean documents (`_id` → `id`, drop `__v` and sensitive fields).
- Validate every external input (`req.body`, `req.params`, `req.query`) with `schema.parse()`; a `ZodError` becomes a 400 automatically. Use `z.infer` for input types and `z.coerce` for query/param numbers.

```ts
// controllers/project.controller.ts
export async function createProject(req: Request, res: Response): Promise<void> {
  const input = createProjectSchema.parse(req.body);
  const project = await projectService.create(input);
  sendSuccess(res, project, 201);
}

// services/project.service.ts
export async function create(input: CreateProjectInput): Promise<ProjectDto> {
  if (await projectRepository.existsByCode(input.code)) {
    throw ApiError.conflict('Project code already in use');
  }
  return toProjectDto(await projectRepository.create(input));
}

// repositories/project.repository.ts
export function existsByCode(code: string): Promise<boolean> {
  return ProjectModel.exists({ code }).then(Boolean);
}
```

❌ `if (project.status === 'closed') throw ...` inside a controller — that rule belongs in the service.
